# Bossa-Style Groove (repertoire plan: st-bossa-groove). An original 16-bar fingerstyle comp on
# Am7 (5x555x) and D7 (x5453x), two bars each, four times, with a one-bar ending on Am7.
# The thumb (P) plays the root on beats 1 and 3: string 6 fret 5 (A) for Am7, string 5 fret 5 (D)
# for D7. The fingers (i, m, a on strings 4, 3 and 2) pluck the upper three notes together in a
# two-bar syncopated pattern, counted in straight eighths:
#   first bar:  beat 1 (with the thumb), the "and" of 2, beat 4
#   second bar: the "and" of 1, beat 3 (with the thumb), the "and" of 3
# Am7 is a first-finger barre at fret 5 with string 5 left unplucked; D7 is fingers 3, 2, 4 and 1
# on strings 5, 4, 3 and 2 (frets 5, 4, 5 and 3). Am7 to D7 is the i-IV7 vamp of A Dorian: in
# the fingers' three notes C stays on string 3 while G falls to F# and E falls to D.
title: Bossa-Style Groove
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original fingerstyle comping study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 7
tags: bossa, latin, fingerstyle, syncopation, seventh chords
tempo: 116
time: 4/4
key: A Dorian

track: Your part
role: lead
